WEBVTT

00:02.335 --> 00:04.003
<i>The Naruhata Branch
Marukane Department Store</i>

00:04.004 --> 00:05.880
<i>was damaged by a Villain.</i>

00:06.464 --> 00:08.633
<i>Currently, they are under reconstruction.</i>

00:09.467 --> 00:13.346
<i>In order to commemorate
the re-opening of the department store,</i>

00:13.930 --> 00:15.973
<i>there will be an event,
and Pop will participate</i>

00:15.974 --> 00:17.475
<i>as a member of an ensemble.</i>

00:18.685 --> 00:20.687
<i>Today, all the members
are meeting together.</i>

00:21.271 --> 00:23.188
<i>I decided to tag along with Pop</i>

00:23.189 --> 00:25.191
<i>as her "manager".</i>

00:31.281 --> 00:33.825
<i>Pop is nervous,
so I can't make her go alone,</i>

00:34.409 --> 00:37.579
<i>and there's no guarantee
that another Villain incident will occur.</i>

00:40.874 --> 00:43.208
<i>Oh, and plus, Master told me</i>

00:43.209 --> 00:45.628
<i>to help her out.</i>

00:49.299 --> 00:50.425
Found you.

00:53.595 --> 00:56.306
Glad to see you doing well.

02:27.021 --> 02:27.896
IDOL

02:27.897 --> 02:29.857
AN OBJECT OF ADMIRATION OR WORSHIP

02:29.858 --> 02:31.650
CELEBRITIES WHO CHARM AUDIENCES

02:31.651 --> 02:33.027
WITH THEIR PERSONALITIES

02:36.239 --> 02:37.824
Hello.

02:38.408 --> 02:39.533
Hello.

02:39.534 --> 02:42.036
Koichi-kun, Pop-chan, welcome.

02:42.620 --> 02:45.164
The meeting will be held
in this conference room, huh?

02:45.165 --> 02:48.625
Yeah. We'll be using this room
on the day of the event too.

02:48.626 --> 02:51.170
Oh, but let me first
introduce you to them.

02:51.796 --> 02:54.883
They're the underground idol duo,
FeatherS.

02:55.466 --> 02:58.386
- I'm Miu of FeatherS.
- I'm Yu.

02:59.470 --> 03:01.638
Nice to meet you. I'm Pop☆Step.

03:01.639 --> 03:03.600
I'm her manager.

03:04.183 --> 03:07.603
The other members will get here soon,

03:07.604 --> 03:09.063
so please wait a little bit.

03:13.443 --> 03:16.904
Did that girl seriously come here
in that tacky outfit?

03:16.905 --> 03:18.615
She has no self-awareness.

03:19.282 --> 03:21.158
Oh, stop that.

03:21.159 --> 03:22.619
But it's true...

03:25.955 --> 03:26.998
Excuse me!

03:31.628 --> 03:33.503
We are here to participate in the event.

03:33.504 --> 03:35.839
We are the Naruhata East High School
Dance Squad.

03:35.840 --> 03:37.591
Welcome.

03:37.592 --> 03:40.302
By the way, your consent form says

03:40.303 --> 03:43.388
that you don't have a particular
costume prepared,

03:43.389 --> 03:45.058
but can we put together something for you?

03:45.642 --> 03:46.768
That is unnecessary.

03:47.352 --> 03:49.728
We, the Naruhata East High School
Dance Squad,

03:49.729 --> 03:52.564
believe that dancing is about
expressing ourselves through movements.

03:52.565 --> 03:55.317
One must master
the mind, technique, and body.

03:55.318 --> 03:58.111
Costumes will only bring down
the quality of our performance.

03:58.112 --> 04:01.032
So, fancy attires are unnecessary!

04:03.618 --> 04:04.702
I've had enough.

04:05.495 --> 04:08.122
We're MAD HATTER. We're a rock band.

04:08.706 --> 04:11.501
We should be creating content
that will shock society.

04:12.085 --> 04:14.837
But we're here to join some recital?

04:15.421 --> 04:18.424
I won't be part
of some lame commercial jingle!

04:19.133 --> 04:22.469
I don't know who the hell you are,
but it seems like

04:22.470 --> 04:24.847
you're not interested, so get out of...

04:27.767 --> 04:29.227
THUMP

04:30.228 --> 04:31.729
Oh crap.

04:33.564 --> 04:35.357
I think I found something

04:35.358 --> 04:37.442
more important to me than rock n' roll.

04:37.443 --> 04:39.195
Hey, what's going on all of a sudden?

04:40.655 --> 04:41.948
I...

04:42.532 --> 04:44.866
- want to be pretty.
- President!

04:44.867 --> 04:48.454
Leave it up to me! I'll make sure
to prepare a pretty costume!

04:50.123 --> 04:52.541
All right.

04:52.542 --> 04:56.170
These are the members of the special group
for the Naruhata Festival.

04:56.754 --> 04:58.797
The band and dancers are all set.

04:58.798 --> 05:02.426
We have to discuss how to combine
FeatherS and Pop☆Step.

05:02.427 --> 05:04.177
If we place Pop in the center,

05:04.178 --> 05:06.013
it'll look more balanced--

05:06.014 --> 05:09.099
Hey! If you do that,
we'll look like backup singers!

05:09.100 --> 05:12.102
Plus, she's not a good singer.

05:12.103 --> 05:13.730
You're right.

05:14.397 --> 05:15.605
<i>Oh no, she agreed with them.</i>

05:15.606 --> 05:20.027
<i>But when it comes to stage presence,
Pop stands out a lot more.</i>

05:20.028 --> 05:23.113
<i>FeatherS, you guys usually perform
at small venues,</i>

05:23.114 --> 05:26.617
<i>so you're not familiar with moves
that make use of big spaces.</i>

05:28.077 --> 05:30.246
Therefore, we'll put this discussion
on hold for now.

05:30.830 --> 05:33.206
In the next coming week,

05:33.207 --> 05:34.541
Pop will practice her singing.

05:34.542 --> 05:37.044
As for FeatherS, you two will learn

05:37.045 --> 05:39.004
dance moves and how to work the stage

05:39.005 --> 05:40.590
from the dance squad.

05:42.884 --> 05:46.387
Training, huh? We won't go easy on you.

05:48.347 --> 05:50.807
One week before the event,

05:50.808 --> 05:53.477
we will assess everyone's condition
and decide on positions.

05:53.478 --> 05:56.480
Then we'll align everything together
and take the stage.

05:56.481 --> 05:57.940
Okay?

05:58.524 --> 06:01.735
Tsukauchi-san, I need to talk to you
regarding the adjustment of the lineup.

06:01.736 --> 06:03.862
Can you also check the equipment list?

06:03.863 --> 06:05.656
Yes, I'll be there right away.

06:06.240 --> 06:09.618
HATTER, can you guys stay behind,
so we can talk about the songs?

06:09.619 --> 06:10.535
Yes.

06:10.536 --> 06:13.205
As for everyone else,
I will keep in touch with you all.

06:13.206 --> 06:14.206
Yes, ma'am.

06:14.207 --> 06:15.958
That's it for today.

06:16.751 --> 06:19.586
Oh, I forgot to mention.

06:19.587 --> 06:20.796
In this event,

06:20.797 --> 06:24.884
all 11 of you are the star of this event.

06:30.223 --> 06:31.933
Makoto-san sent the audio file.

06:32.517 --> 06:35.103
- I have to practice.
- You're really fired up.

06:35.728 --> 06:39.022
It would be great if you could sing
in the center, huh?

06:39.023 --> 06:41.274
Yeah, because in my case,

06:41.275 --> 06:43.401
if I'm leaping around on the side,

06:43.402 --> 06:45.905
I'll look really out of place.

06:47.740 --> 06:50.952
You can use this place
all you want for practice.

07:03.506 --> 07:05.383
Speed it up, you sloths!

07:06.175 --> 07:08.427
Put a pep in your step!

07:29.866 --> 07:32.285
EAST HIGH

07:33.411 --> 07:34.829
Keep going!

07:37.623 --> 07:40.459
<i>How's it going, hey hey</i>

07:40.460 --> 07:43.421
<i>Are you doing well, hey hey</i>

07:44.005 --> 07:46.923
<i>Everyone come together</i>

07:46.924 --> 07:49.551
<i>And join us</i>

07:49.552 --> 07:50.886
Um...

07:50.887 --> 07:52.971
I'm going to sleep soon.

07:52.972 --> 07:55.265
No, you have to listen to me!

07:55.266 --> 07:56.976
What...

08:04.442 --> 08:06.152
It's another monster-like Villain!

08:06.736 --> 08:09.155
This time, it's something
that would come out in a movie!

08:10.281 --> 08:11.699
<i>He is</i>

08:12.283 --> 08:15.995
<i>Captain Celebrity!</i>

08:24.462 --> 08:25.921
I'd like to say one thing

08:25.922 --> 08:27.548
to my audience here.

08:28.466 --> 08:31.343
Marukane and C.C's collaboration event,

08:31.344 --> 08:33.929
the Naruhata Festival,
is happening in ten days.

08:33.930 --> 08:36.682
Please look up "Naru Fest".

08:37.683 --> 08:40.394
The Naru Fest will be happening soon!

08:40.978 --> 08:44.941
Here are the flyers! Take the flyers!

08:45.983 --> 08:48.819
<i>Marukane, Marukane</i>

08:49.403 --> 08:52.031
<i>Let's go to Marukane</i>

08:56.786 --> 08:57.994
ONE WEEK BEFORE THE EVENT

08:57.995 --> 08:59.454
What? Injured?

08:59.455 --> 09:02.541
During the dance practice?

09:02.542 --> 09:03.668
Yeah.

09:04.377 --> 09:05.920
Thankfully, it's a minor sprain,

09:06.504 --> 09:09.589
so she'll be able
to take the stage next week,

09:09.590 --> 09:12.134
but she won't be able to run or dance.

09:12.969 --> 09:14.470
This is all my fault.

09:15.054 --> 09:17.765
No, I'm the one responsible
for this project.

09:18.349 --> 09:21.393
I thought everyone would get fired up
with something to work towards.

09:21.394 --> 09:23.479
But it backfired.

09:24.188 --> 09:25.106
We have no choice.

09:25.690 --> 09:27.857
We can put Pop in the center,

09:27.858 --> 09:30.735
with FeatherS on either side of her,
as they try to stay in place.

09:30.736 --> 09:32.529
Or we can take out Miyu

09:32.530 --> 09:35.491
and create a new duo with Pop and Yu.

09:37.535 --> 09:39.996
I practiced so much...

09:40.621 --> 09:42.039
Miyu-chan.

09:45.209 --> 09:46.752
What? Place Miyu in the center?

09:47.336 --> 09:49.713
Because she can't move around much, right?

09:49.714 --> 09:52.508
I guess your idea might work.

09:53.092 --> 09:55.176
<i>The center is positioned
at the middle of the stage.</i>

09:55.177 --> 09:58.639
<i>Whoever's in the center won't look awkward
even if she doesn't move around.</i>

09:59.223 --> 10:02.058
<i>If Yu moves around twice as much,
the contrast between her</i>

10:02.059 --> 10:03.853
<i>and Miyu will keep the audience engaged.</i>

10:04.854 --> 10:07.272
<i>When things slow down
during transitions and such,</i>

10:07.273 --> 10:10.401
<i>Pop can leap around
and distract the audience.</i>

10:10.985 --> 10:13.361
Pop and Yu will have to take on
the extra burden,

10:13.362 --> 10:15.323
but will you guys be all right?

10:16.741 --> 10:20.703
If I got injured, I'd be someone
who can't sing or leap.

10:21.287 --> 10:23.414
But you guys are good singers,

10:23.998 --> 10:27.877
and I'm good at leaping
and jumping in the air.

10:29.712 --> 10:32.798
So, let's all do what we do best!

10:37.011 --> 10:38.136
All right.

10:38.137 --> 10:40.388
Let's all discuss our positions.

10:40.389 --> 10:41.306
Yes.

10:41.307 --> 10:44.309
- She's a nice girl.
- Yeah.

10:44.310 --> 10:45.686
She sure is.

10:46.270 --> 10:49.231
Let's take advantage
of Pop-chan's vertical movements.

10:49.815 --> 10:53.944
<i>The squad president cut her hair. I bet
she feels responsible for what happened.</i>

10:54.528 --> 10:56.364
<i>"You look good with short hair too."</i>

10:56.864 --> 10:58.782
<i>No way I can say that right now.</i>

10:58.783 --> 11:00.909
<i>I'll tell her
once our performance is over.</i>

11:00.910 --> 11:04.120
Oh wow, you cut your hair?

11:04.121 --> 11:06.123
You cut off a lot, huh?

11:06.707 --> 11:09.043
You look good with short hair too!

11:13.255 --> 11:15.132
- Oh?
- Idiot.

11:23.557 --> 11:26.936
Collaboration between Captain Celebrity
and local performers, huh?

11:27.520 --> 11:30.314
"Heroes will make
surprise guest appearances too."

11:31.232 --> 11:32.400
Whatever.

11:32.983 --> 11:35.068
If Heroes are going to make
surprise appearances,

11:35.069 --> 11:38.406
a Villain should make
a surprise appearance too.

11:42.243 --> 11:45.496
Oh, you agree too?

11:47.790 --> 11:49.792
Pop-chan...

11:50.418 --> 11:55.214
Yeah, let's go cheer on Pop-chan.

11:58.342 --> 12:05.306
<i>Naruhata, Naruhata</i>

12:05.307 --> 12:08.935
<i>Naruhata's</i>

12:08.936 --> 12:12.648
<i>Neon signs are cloudy</i>

12:13.274 --> 12:17.193
<i>Because of the tears</i>

12:17.194 --> 12:22.324
<i>Falling like rain</i>

12:25.244 --> 12:28.538
That performance just now
was by the Enka Master

12:28.539 --> 12:30.457
Harusaburo Nanboku,

12:30.458 --> 12:32.041
singing his hit song,

12:32.042 --> 12:34.503
"Yearning For Naruhata".

12:35.087 --> 12:38.339
Sorry to deliver this sad news
when everyone is having fun,

12:38.340 --> 12:42.219
but this brings an end
to the afternoon portion of this event!

12:42.803 --> 12:45.388
Heroes will make guest appearances
during the evening event.

12:45.389 --> 12:48.224
First performance this evening
will be Naruhata's very first

12:48.225 --> 12:51.895
ultra-fresh song and dance unit

12:51.896 --> 12:54.315
FeatherHATS.

12:58.194 --> 12:59.278
The afternoon portion ended.

13:00.029 --> 13:01.822
There's 30 minutes until we go on stage.

13:02.907 --> 13:05.408
What have I agreed to do?

13:05.409 --> 13:07.285
What's going on?

13:07.286 --> 13:08.495
It'll be all right.

13:08.496 --> 13:09.747
Don't try to make us feel better!

13:10.915 --> 13:12.249
Calm down, everyone.

13:12.750 --> 13:14.418
Remember how much we all practiced.

13:15.002 --> 13:16.879
All of our hard work will not let us down!

13:17.505 --> 13:19.088
Let's all take a deep breath.

13:19.089 --> 13:21.842
- Who is that?
- She's the president of the dance squad!

13:22.635 --> 13:25.053
Oh, now that you mention it,
I can kind of see it.

13:25.054 --> 13:26.430
We can do this!

13:27.014 --> 13:30.267
<i>You're beautiful.
My Cinderella with a bob.</i>

13:30.851 --> 13:34.020
<i>Today I will use my guitar
to make you forget the time.</i>

13:34.021 --> 13:36.523
<i>Once time stops,</i>

13:36.524 --> 13:39.359
<i>that transformation will become a magic
that lasts forever.</i>

13:39.360 --> 13:42.695
Wow, President! Anybody can look good
with the right clothes, huh?

13:42.696 --> 13:45.407
Koichi! That's not a compliment!

13:48.369 --> 13:50.495
Oh, is that right?

13:50.496 --> 13:52.039
You're the worst.

13:53.165 --> 13:56.335
Very nice! Very nice, you guys!

13:56.835 --> 14:00.213
You guys are perfect.
The epitome of youth.

14:00.214 --> 14:02.924
She's Midnight, the R-rated Hero!

14:02.925 --> 14:05.302
This is amazing. And she's so sexy!

14:06.136 --> 14:07.971
I'm so sorry

14:07.972 --> 14:11.808
we couldn't prepare you
your own private waiting room.

14:11.809 --> 14:12.768
No problem.

14:13.352 --> 14:15.728
This feels like I'm backstage
at a school festival.

14:15.729 --> 14:17.106
I kind of like it.

14:18.566 --> 14:21.277
Oh, good evening, Midnight.

14:22.027 --> 14:24.947
Oh, wait. "Evening"? "Midnight"?

14:27.491 --> 14:29.033
It's so confusing!

14:29.034 --> 14:30.159
Shut up, Yamada.

14:30.160 --> 14:32.203
No, no, it's not Yamada.

14:32.204 --> 14:34.205
Please call me Mic.

14:34.206 --> 14:36.542
My name is Present Mic.

14:37.126 --> 14:40.337
Sorry. By the way, Yamada,
where's Aizawa today?

14:40.921 --> 14:43.089
<i>Did you tell him that all the Heroes</i>

14:43.090 --> 14:45.258
<i>involved in the mass
Villain outbreak incident</i>

14:45.259 --> 14:46.885
<i>should attend this event?</i>

14:46.886 --> 14:50.013
Although all the famous ones
said they can't come.

14:50.014 --> 14:53.349
- So stupid.
- I can't reschedule my shift.

14:53.350 --> 14:55.894
He can't attend.

14:55.895 --> 14:57.020
Of course,

14:57.021 --> 14:59.647
I covered all the bases.
I told him, and he said,

14:59.648 --> 15:01.650
"I'll go if I can."

15:03.694 --> 15:06.071
<i>That means he's not going to come.</i>

15:07.615 --> 15:11.243
Yeah, yeah, I'm going.
I'm heading there now.

15:11.827 --> 15:12.827
I'm hanging up now.

15:12.828 --> 15:14.955
This conversation is wasting my time.

15:16.916 --> 15:19.960
But honestly, I don't really care to go.

15:20.544 --> 15:23.630
I'm not the type
to make myself a public figure.

15:23.631 --> 15:25.882
Plus, hosting an event
for a town renewal project

15:25.883 --> 15:27.634
is not rational at all.

15:27.635 --> 15:29.887
If they want to improve the community,
just gather donations.

15:30.971 --> 15:32.430
What a hassle.

15:32.431 --> 15:35.224
If only a Villain would appear
somewhere around here,

15:35.225 --> 15:37.727
I'd have an excuse
to skip out on the event.

15:37.728 --> 15:39.688
It's a Villain!

15:41.231 --> 15:42.983
I don't know who it is...

15:45.027 --> 15:47.404
But whoever it is, listened to my request.

15:51.700 --> 15:53.534
Help us!

15:53.535 --> 15:55.162
Pop.

15:55.746 --> 15:57.581
He's having trouble
maneuvering his big body.

15:59.959 --> 16:01.710
He was not born this way.

16:02.294 --> 16:04.046
Is this a Transformation-type Quirk?

16:04.630 --> 16:07.383
Or is he an Instant Villain?

16:08.050 --> 16:10.052
A lot of those appear around here.

16:17.977 --> 16:19.352
Excuse me.

16:19.353 --> 16:22.313
I'm Pro Hero Eraser Head.

16:22.314 --> 16:25.359
It seems like your Quirk
is going out of control.

16:25.985 --> 16:28.070
Sorry, but I'm going
to keep you restrained

16:28.696 --> 16:30.322
until the police arrive.

16:33.867 --> 16:37.871
<i>I used Erasure,
but his form hasn't changed.</i>

16:38.455 --> 16:40.415
<i>This isn't a temporary "Transformation"?</i>

16:40.416 --> 16:42.418
<i>Is this his natural form?</i>

16:42.960 --> 16:44.628
<i>He escaped from the Binding!</i>

16:45.212 --> 16:46.797
It must be mucus on his skin.

16:55.973 --> 16:57.057
<i>Attacks will be ineffective.</i>

16:57.641 --> 16:59.601
<i>He's a lot trickier than I expected.</i>

17:00.686 --> 17:01.603
But...

17:07.317 --> 17:08.902
if his form won't change,

17:09.611 --> 17:12.156
I can just trap him in a net.

17:20.914 --> 17:22.499
Pop-chan.

17:23.000 --> 17:24.751
That's right.

17:24.752 --> 17:27.420
Make sure Pop-chan
understands how you feel.

17:27.421 --> 17:29.923
You can do it.

17:30.549 --> 17:31.800
He's...

17:32.342 --> 17:34.510
QUIRK - ELECTRIC EEL

17:34.511 --> 17:36.805
Oh crap. The flash is blinding me.

17:55.908 --> 17:57.450
I'm impressed.

17:57.451 --> 17:59.660
That was as powerful as lightning.

17:59.661 --> 18:01.413
Teruo-kun, you did very well.

18:02.122 --> 18:04.332
I can get a really good sample from you.

18:04.333 --> 18:05.876
I have to go retrieve it.

18:07.086 --> 18:09.254
But before I do that,

18:09.838 --> 18:12.090
I'll send tons of Trigger to that venue

18:12.091 --> 18:15.803
where people are panicking
over the power outage.

18:19.807 --> 18:21.349
<i>Hachisuka-kun.</i>

18:21.350 --> 18:22.934
<i>As I mentioned to you before,</i>

18:22.935 --> 18:25.895
<i>your actions aren't very cost effective.</i>

18:25.896 --> 18:27.980
<i>Already as it is,
bringing out test specimens</i>

18:27.981 --> 18:30.108
<i>involves lots of risks.</i>

18:30.109 --> 18:32.985
<i>Worst case scenario,
we might not be able to proceed</i>

18:32.986 --> 18:35.113
<i>with our experiments in Naruhata anymore.</i>

18:35.114 --> 18:38.825
Who cares if I have
a little fun with this.

18:38.826 --> 18:42.161
Not to mention that I hate being lectured.

18:42.162 --> 18:44.164
You hate being lectured, huh?

18:46.250 --> 18:47.459
Couldn't agree more.

18:48.127 --> 18:51.170
I don't think anyone likes being lectured.

18:51.171 --> 18:53.422
Especially at your age,

18:53.423 --> 18:56.135
no one wants
to be ordered around by others.

18:56.718 --> 18:59.512
In that sense, I'm pretty understanding.

18:59.513 --> 19:01.974
Let's make this quick.

19:02.558 --> 19:05.435
What is it all of a sudden, you old man?

19:08.438 --> 19:10.439
Let's go home, Tamao.

19:10.440 --> 19:12.400
Mom's waiting.

19:12.401 --> 19:14.777
What are you saying, Old Man?

19:14.778 --> 19:16.988
"Go home"? "Waiting"?

19:16.989 --> 19:18.906
It's making no sense to me.

19:18.907 --> 19:20.325
Shut up, bee user.

19:20.951 --> 19:24.037
I'm not talking to you.
I'm talking to Tamao Oguro,

19:25.289 --> 19:27.374
my daughter!

19:33.839 --> 19:36.091
Is that why you're using a stun gun?

19:36.675 --> 19:38.886
So that you don't injure your daughter?

19:44.099 --> 19:45.058
I see...

19:46.727 --> 19:49.897
That's so weak!

19:53.775 --> 19:56.402
There's no point if you use your fist!

19:56.403 --> 19:59.656
If possible,
I'd rather not use this stun gun.

20:00.240 --> 20:02.742
After all, this is a special stun gun.

20:02.743 --> 20:05.494
High voltage and high amperage.

20:05.495 --> 20:08.331
A light brush against the arm or leg
will numb your entire body.

20:08.332 --> 20:11.335
If it touches your chest,
your heart will stop.

20:12.377 --> 20:13.921
You're bluffing.

20:16.757 --> 20:18.508
You're releasing the working bees.

20:19.092 --> 20:20.718
They're flying syringes.

20:20.719 --> 20:24.263
Is it filled with poison,
anesthesia, or stimulants?

20:24.264 --> 20:26.225
No matter what it is,

20:26.934 --> 20:30.145
it'll be quicker for me
to take down the Queen Bee.

20:35.234 --> 20:36.275
Idiot!

20:36.276 --> 20:38.236
They're a special kind.

20:38.237 --> 20:41.948
<i>You're right, what's inside
is dangerous. It's explosives.</i>

20:41.949 --> 20:45.077
Let all the Bomb Bees attack you!

20:53.168 --> 20:55.045
I blew you up into pieces!

21:01.468 --> 21:02.970
That was a bluff.

21:04.972 --> 21:08.100
Only the first one had explosives.

21:09.101 --> 21:11.561
Rest were filled with fireworks
for a threatening effect.

21:12.145 --> 21:14.522
The explosives take a toll on you,
the host, huh?

21:14.523 --> 21:17.233
There's a limit to the number
of Bomb Bees you can use.

21:17.234 --> 21:20.194
And the fact that you resorted to bluffing

21:20.195 --> 21:23.406
means you no longer have
an effective means of attack.

21:23.407 --> 21:26.117
That's what I found out so far.

21:26.118 --> 21:27.661
Damn Old Man!

21:29.830 --> 21:32.624
Keep that cocky attitude
to yourself, idiot!

21:35.002 --> 21:37.879
First, it's fireworks,
and now you're playing tag?

21:46.346 --> 21:48.015
That's fine with me.

21:52.269 --> 21:55.856
Let's see if you can run away from me.

23:26.822 --> 23:28.697
<i>While the event was taking place,</i>

23:28.698 --> 23:30.534
<i>a fierce battle was taking place.</i>

23:31.034 --> 23:32.994
<i>A Vigilante versus a Villain.</i>

23:33.620 --> 23:35.413
<i>And a father versus his daughter.</i>

23:36.164 --> 23:38.374
<i>Next episode, "Goodbye to Dad."</i>

23:38.375 --> 23:40.417
<i>The plot thickens.</i>

23:40.418 --> 23:41.962
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita
